<title>USA: North Carolina advances stadium tax referendum.</title>
<headline>North Carolina advances stadium tax referendum.</headline>
<dateline>RALEIGH, N.C. 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>North Carolina's House Finance Committee approved a referendum allowing Forsyth and Guildford counties to vote on a new tax for a baseball stadium.</p>
<p>The proposal passed 31-11 Tuesday. If voters approve in a May referendum, the counties would levy a one percent tax on restaurant meals and a 50-cent tax on major league baseball tickets for up to 25 years.</p>
<p>Tax revenues would be used to pay debt service on $140 million of municipal bonds for the $220 million stadium. Private investors would fund the rest.</p>
<p>The stadium would be built near Kernersville on the Forsyth-Guildford county line if the region wins a baseball franchise.</p>
<p>((--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013))</p>
</text>
